From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: wireless: uwe5622: do not log expected conditions at error level

Three messages fire during normal operation at pr_err level and drown
real errors in dmesg:

- sprdwl_intf_find_lut_index() logs "ctx_id = %d, sm_state = %d,
  bssid =..." for every multicast/broadcast frame sent while the
  station is not associated (no peer entry), dozens per minute with
  IPv6/mDNS traffic. Falling back to LUT index 0 is the intended path.
- __sprdwl_cmd_getbuf() logs "cant't get vif" for the commands sent
  while the interface is being opened, before the vif exists; the code
  deliberately defaults to SPRDWL_MODE_NONE ("open new device") there.
- The firmware ini path is informational.

Move the first two to wl_debug (still printed with sprdwl_debug_level
raised) and the ini path to pr_info.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/cmdevt.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@
 	if (cmd_id >= WIFI_CMD_OPEN) {
 		vif = ctx_id_to_vif(priv, ctx_id);
 		if (!vif)
-			wl_err("%s cant't get vif, ctx_id: %d\n",
+			wl_debug("%s cant't get vif, ctx_id: %d\n",
 			       __func__, ctx_id);
 		else
 			mode =  vif->mode;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/rf_marlin3.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/rf_marlin3.c
@@ -485,6 +485,6 @@
 	sprintf(conf_name, "wifi_%8x_%dant.ini", chipid, ant);
 	strcat(path_buf, conf_name);
 
-	pr_err("wifi ini path = %s\n", path_buf);
+	pr_info("wifi ini path = %s\n", path_buf);
 	return wifi_nvm_parse(path_buf, (void *)p);
 }
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/wl_intf.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/uwe5622/unisocwifi/wl_intf.c
@@ -681,7 +681,7 @@
 		break;
 	}
 
-	wl_err("ctx_id = %d, sm_state = %d, bssid =%pM\n",
+	wl_debug("ctx_id = %d, sm_state = %d, bssid =%pM\n",
 			vif->ctx_id, vif->sm_state, intf->skb_da);
 
 	return ret;
